The method getJsonPath is used to extract the name field from the JSON response, which has been deserialized so you can work with it easily.

Why is this important?
Serialization is used to send data (usually in a format like JSON) to a server when you want to create, update, or send data through an API.

Deserialization is used to receive and convert that data back into a format that your program can understand and use.

To summarize:
Serialization: Converting an object to JSON (to send to the server).

Deserialization: Converting JSON back to an object (to read the response from the server).

In your code, these processes help interact with a server by transforming complex Java objects into JSON and vice versa, making it easier to communicate with external systems.




